00:35:56,166 --> 00:36:01,336
(Kim Jong Eun does not have a date tomorrow.)

787
00:36:01,736 --> 00:36:05,446
I think I'm still thinking about what I should do.

788
00:36:11,986 --> 00:36:16,426
(Han Do Gon does not have a date tomorrow.)

789
00:36:16,656 --> 00:36:20,226
I've been looking only at one person this whole time.

790
00:36:20,656 --> 00:36:23,966
Of course, I also want...

791
00:36:24,326 --> 00:36:27,196
the person I like to like me back since I'm human.

792
00:36:27,936 --> 00:36:30,636
I also felt a bit bitter.

793
00:36:34,136 --> 00:36:35,905
(Kim Ryun Gi has a date...)

794
00:36:35,906 --> 00:36:37,806
(with Seo Ro Bin tomorrow.)

795
00:36:38,176 --> 00:36:39,746
I felt really good.

796
00:36:40,046 --> 00:36:43,815
I could confirm that Ro Bin...

797
00:36:43,816 --> 00:36:45,256
also had positive feelings about me.

798
00:36:49,786 --> 00:36:51,185
(Seo Ro Bin has a date...)

799
00:36:51,186 --> 00:36:52,456
(with Kim Ryun Gi tomorrow.)

800
00:36:53,026 --> 00:36:54,026
What?

801
00:36:54,027 --> 00:36:55,796
- It's something else.
- Ro Bin.

802
00:36:56,226 --> 00:36:57,366
The result.

803
00:36:57,796 --> 00:37:00,566
I was very grateful.

804
00:37:00,866 --> 00:37:03,106
On the other side, I wanted to figure out...

805
00:37:03,336 --> 00:37:05,736
what the excitement toward Ryun Gi was about.

806
00:37:08,106 --> 00:37:09,905
(What feelings will remain...)

807
00:37:09,906 --> 00:37:12,306
(between certainty and confirmation?)

808
00:37:16,046 --> 00:37:19,315
(Kang Min Young does not have a date tomorrow.)

809
00:37:19,316 --> 00:37:20,486
I felt,

810
00:37:20,556 --> 00:37:23,486
"How could he not allocate time to me even once?"

811
00:37:23,986 --> 00:37:25,026
At the same time,

812
00:37:25,256 --> 00:37:26,726
I realized how it felt.

813
00:37:27,026 --> 00:37:29,826
I also don't give false hope to someone I'm not interested in.

814
00:37:31,066 --> 00:37:34,435
Seon Ho is like that as well.

815
00:37:34,436 --> 00:37:35,836
I could understand it so well,

816
00:37:35,996 --> 00:37:38,106
so I wasn't upset.

817
00:37:43,946 --> 00:37:45,545
(Jung Ye Ji has a date...)

818
00:37:45,546 --> 00:37:47,316
(with Kim Seon Ho tomorrow.)

819
00:37:50,846 --> 00:37:53,256
I was relieved to know...

820
00:37:53,556 --> 00:37:55,856
that he allocated some time to me.

821
00:37:59,126 --> 00:38:01,156
It's such a relief.

822
00:38:01,896 --> 00:38:04,766
It's a bit different from what I thought.

823
00:38:07,066 --> 00:38:08,195
(Kim Na Young has a date...)

824
00:38:08,196 --> 00:38:10,065
(with Kim Seon Ho tomorrow.)

825
00:38:10,066 --> 00:38:11,166
Whose is this?

826
00:38:11,906 --> 00:38:13,175
- Isn't this yours?
- Yes.

827
00:38:13,176 --> 00:38:14,806
You received a text.

828
00:38:15,036 --> 00:38:16,145
So...

829
00:38:16,146 --> 00:38:17,646
(Sighing)

830
00:38:18,176 --> 00:38:22,276
(Ye Ji read Na Young's text by coincidence.)

831
00:38:23,016 --> 00:38:24,346
- Did she see it?
- Hold on!

832
00:38:26,116 --> 00:38:27,116
Did she see it?

833
00:38:28,216 --> 00:38:29,786
Did she see the text?

834
00:38:30,056 --> 00:38:31,355
Goodness.

835
00:38:31,356 --> 00:38:32,656
(She's terrified.)

836
00:38:33,356 --> 00:38:35,295
(They can't believe it.)

837
00:38:35,296 --> 00:38:37,166
Why did you leave your phone there?

838
00:38:37,596 --> 00:38:39,196
It's an important moment!

839
00:38:39,296 --> 00:38:40,836
Why did she read it?

840
00:38:41,196 --> 00:38:42,765
What are we going to do?

841
00:38:42,766 --> 00:38:44,436
How could this happen?

842
00:38:48,076 --> 00:38:52,106
(Seon Ho's time reached the two women.)

843
00:38:54,076 --> 00:38:55,376
This is crazy.

844
00:39:02,186 --> 00:39:05,456
I could feel that Ye Ji was bothered by me.

845
00:39:06,356 --> 00:39:10,026
I'm going to do my best at the date.

846
00:39:10,296 --> 00:39:11,895
I'll only think about Seon Ho...

847
00:39:11,896 --> 00:39:14,936
at the date.

848
00:39:15,466 --> 00:39:17,736
You never know how things will end up.

849
00:39:18,906 --> 00:39:20,575
Honestly, who would feel good?

850
00:39:20,576 --> 00:39:22,536
The person I have feelings for...

851
00:39:22,876 --> 00:39:24,146
allocated his time...

852
00:39:24,706 --> 00:39:27,146
to someone else and went on a date.

853
00:39:27,316 --> 00:39:29,146
But now, I think the depth of it...

854
00:39:29,476 --> 00:39:31,346
is different.

855
00:39:32,116 --> 00:39:33,985
It could be beyond wanting to get to know the person.

856
00:39:33,986 --> 00:39:37,886
He might have feelings for her now.

857
00:39:38,556 --> 00:39:39,756
What if...

858
00:39:40,756 --> 00:39:42,526
things really change?

859
00:39:50,006 --> 00:39:52,005
(Kim Seon Ho has a date...)

860
00:39:52,006 --> 00:39:55,276
(with Kim Na Young and Jung Ye Ji tomorrow.)

861
00:39:56,906 --> 00:39:59,676
I felt conflicted and troubled.

862
00:40:01,176 --> 00:40:03,846
What will happen tomorrow? What should I do?

863
00:40:04,886 --> 00:40:06,386
Will things get certain tomorrow?

864
00:40:12,226 --> 00:40:14,556
This might be exciting and nice to someone else,

865
00:40:14,996 --> 00:40:18,266
but honestly, it's a hard time for me.

866
00:40:34,646 --> 00:40:38,915
(A night of thoughts trailing off...)

867
00:40:38,916 --> 00:40:43,986
(in the midst of unknown emotions)

868
00:40:45,766 --> 00:40:47,805
(The girls' room without Ye Ji)

869
00:40:47,806 --> 00:40:49,086
I need to go to bed early today.

870
00:40:49,806 --> 00:40:51,776
- I don't care anymore.
- What's wrong?

871
00:40:52,436 --> 00:40:53,505
My heart fluttered...

872
00:40:53,506 --> 00:40:54,622
- for the first time.
- What?

873
00:40:54,646 --> 00:40:55,705
My heart fluttered...

874
00:40:55,706 --> 00:40:56,775
- for the first time.
- Really?

875
00:40:56,776 --> 00:40:58,176
- Yes.
- Awesome.

876
00:40:59,146 --> 00:41:01,386
What was it that made your heart flutter?

877
00:41:01,486 --> 00:41:02,516
The thing is...

878
00:41:03,146 --> 00:41:04,456
(Glancing)

879
00:41:05,056 --> 00:41:07,826
My heart fluttered when we first met.

880
00:41:07,986 --> 00:41:08,986
Our hearts fluttered for each other.

881
00:41:08,986 --> 00:41:09,986
Seriously?

882
00:41:11,026 --> 00:41:12,856
- It's like...
- Oh, my gosh!

883
00:41:13,296 --> 00:41:14,325
What's more...

884
00:41:14,326 --> 00:41:16,426
(Na Young's feelings grew after the date.)

885
00:41:16,766 --> 00:41:17,766
And so...

886
00:41:21,966 --> 00:41:22,966
It made you happy?

887
00:41:24,306 --> 00:41:27,106
(Na Young can't hide her feelings.)

888
00:41:27,406 --> 00:41:29,106
Seon Ho is Mr. Popular.

889
00:41:30,876 --> 00:41:32,545
- Maybe it was the date.
- Sorry?

890
00:41:32,546 --> 00:41:34,185
I took the bus right in front of it,

891
00:41:34,186 --> 00:41:35,626
right in front of the traffic light.

892
00:41:35,816 --> 00:41:37,116
Did you take the bus?

893
00:41:37,216 --> 00:41:38,586
We took a city bus tour.

894
00:41:39,186 --> 00:41:41,585
A city bus tour? That sounds fun.

895
00:41:41,586 --> 00:41:43,256
- I'm jealous.
- It was really...

896
00:41:43,886 --> 00:41:44,895
Yes.

897
00:41:44,896 --> 00:41:48,765
It wasn't all that dramatic until now.

898
00:41:48,766 --> 00:41:49,826
- Is that so?
- Yes.

899
00:41:50,066 --> 00:41:52,965
Everything was the same. It's different every single time.

900
00:41:52,966 --> 00:41:56,206
- Really?
- My dates were kind of...

901
00:41:56,306 --> 00:41:58,606
I had 2 dates on the 1st day and the next day.

902
00:41:59,006 --> 00:42:00,236
I had two dates.

903
00:42:00,536 --> 00:42:03,206
He was someone I was most curious about.

904
00:42:03,576 --> 00:42:05,416
Are you all going on a date tomorrow?

905
00:42:06,716 --> 00:42:08,585
- I'm not.
- I am.

906
00:42:08,586 --> 00:42:10,446
- I am.
- I'll be home all alone.

907
00:42:10,956 --> 00:42:12,156
What about you?

908
00:42:12,256 --> 00:42:13,286
I am too.

909
00:42:15,786 --> 00:42:16,786
(Glancing)

910
00:42:16,787 --> 00:42:18,555
It's hard to guess who my date will be.

911
00:42:18,556 --> 00:42:20,096
I wonder who everyone's dates are.

912
00:42:20,726 --> 00:42:21,726
I know.

913
00:42:22,126 --> 00:42:24,366
- I'm curious.
- Who's my date tomorrow?

914
00:42:28,006 --> 00:42:30,465
(The late-night snack arrived.)

915
00:42:30,466 --> 00:42:31,475
What's this?

916
00:42:31,476 --> 00:42:32,835
- It looks good.
- Oh, my gosh.

917
00:42:32,836 --> 00:42:35,276
- I'm dying to dig in.
- Same here.

918
00:42:36,376 --> 00:42:40,276
(Everyone has gathered in the playroom.)

919
00:42:41,716 --> 00:42:42,746
What is it?

920
00:42:44,286 --> 00:42:45,286
What are you looking for?

921
00:42:46,316 --> 00:42:47,756
I'm going to have leftover wine.

922
00:42:48,856 --> 00:42:51,095
Wait. Are you going to drink the leftover wine?

923
00:42:51,096 --> 00:42:52,826
- I'll bring it with me.
- Get me a glass.

924
00:42:54,326 --> 00:42:56,326
(Staring)

925
00:42:58,266 --> 00:43:01,606
(Seon Ho brought some wine to have with Na Young.)

926
00:43:02,666 --> 00:43:03,705
Thank you.

927
00:43:03,706 --> 00:43:04,835
It's 13.5 percent.

928
00:43:04,836 --> 00:43:07,005
The drink I had earlier...

929
00:43:07,006 --> 00:43:08,476
was around 15 percent.

930
00:43:10,946 --> 00:43:11,975
You're tired, aren't you?

931
00:43:11,976 --> 00:43:14,016
I'm a little tired, but it's okay.

932
00:43:14,516 --> 00:43:17,216
I need to get some sleep tonight.

933
00:43:17,786 --> 00:43:18,915
Nice.

934
00:43:18,916 --> 00:43:21,226
(Seon Ho pours a glass of wine for Na Young.)

935
00:43:23,526 --> 00:43:26,046
- I've been wanting to try it.
- Are we going outside tomorrow?

936
00:43:27,466 --> 00:43:31,336
(The two continue to drink at the House.)

937
00:43:32,996 --> 00:43:35,205
Wait. This is way better.

938
00:43:35,206 --> 00:43:36,206
Right?

939
00:43:36,466 --> 00:43:37,536
It's sweeter.

940
00:43:38,306 --> 00:43:40,605
- This wine is less sweet for me.
- Am I...

941
00:43:40,606 --> 00:43:41,675
Am I drunk right now?

942
00:43:41,676 --> 00:43:43,546
- It's fine.
- No, it's not.

943
00:43:43,876 --> 00:43:45,815
It smells less of alcohol.

944
00:43:45,816 --> 00:43:46,816
Is that so?

945
00:43:47,146 --> 00:43:48,286
It's slightly sweet.

946
00:43:55,126 --> 00:43:59,226
(Ye Ji can't join in on the two's conversation.)

947
00:44:00,356 --> 00:44:01,866
Right now...

948
00:44:02,826 --> 00:44:03,866
Take a photo?

949
00:44:04,966 --> 00:44:06,496
(Take a photo right now.)

950
00:44:07,296 --> 00:44:08,465
(Seon Ho spotted Do Gon, who fell asleep.)

951
00:44:08,466 --> 00:44:09,636
Make him look cool.

952
00:44:10,036 --> 00:44:11,505
- He's a model for sure.
- A model is different.

953
00:44:11,506 --> 00:44:12,536
Totally.

954
00:44:13,376 --> 00:44:14,975
- Do Gon's nose is really...
- Pretty.

955
00:44:14,976 --> 00:44:16,306
- Exactly.
- It's really pretty.

956
00:44:16,406 --> 00:44:17,475
I'm jealous of his nose.

957
00:44:17,476 --> 00:44:19,176
- Me too.
- He reminds me of Gong Yoo.

958
00:44:20,676 --> 00:44:21,685
What?

959
00:44:21,686 --> 00:44:23,616
He said you looked like Gong Yoo. Good for you.

960
00:44:26,056 --> 00:44:27,786
Na Young's nose is pretty too.

961
00:44:28,356 --> 00:44:30,185
- Me?
- It's sharp.

962
00:44:30,186 --> 00:44:31,526
My nose is a little round.

963
00:44:32,056 --> 00:44:33,526
It's kind of bent.

964
00:44:34,726 --> 00:44:37,466
Oh, no. He said it right in front of her.

965
00:44:38,696 --> 00:44:40,566
Hold on a minute.

966
00:44:41,006 --> 00:44:42,305
To bring up...

967
00:44:42,306 --> 00:44:44,035
- Na Young in public...
- Exactly.

968
00:44:44,036 --> 00:44:45,596
- It's a first, right?
- What do we do?

969
00:44:45,736 --> 00:44:46,736
Bringing her up in public...

970
00:44:46,737 --> 00:44:47,745
- is a first, right?
- Yes.

971
00:44:47,746 --> 00:44:49,346
Seon Ho just crossed the line.

972
00:44:49,506 --> 00:44:51,815
With the relationship still unresolved,

973
00:44:51,816 --> 00:44:53,815
I don't think it was right for him...

974
00:44:53,816 --> 00:44:55,485
- Right.
- to tell Ye Ji...

975
00:44:55,486 --> 00:44:58,515
where they are right now through "Na Young's nose is pretty too."

976
00:44:58,516 --> 00:45:00,215
I'm sure it didn't mean too much.

977
00:45:00,216 --> 00:45:02,025
He said it because her nose was actually pretty.

978
00:45:02,026 --> 00:45:04,156
But saying it out of the blue...

979
00:45:04,256 --> 00:45:06,926
and while everyone was there was...

980
00:45:07,826 --> 00:45:08,826
This is practically a horror movie.

981
00:45:08,827 --> 00:45:09,942
- A horror movie.
- Exactly.

982
00:45:09,966 --> 00:45:10,966
Really.

983
00:45:17,306 --> 00:45:19,606
I was quite upset about it.

984
00:45:19,706 --> 00:45:21,376
The two looked close.

985
00:45:21,846 --> 00:45:24,716
They kept drinking in the House.

986
00:45:25,416 --> 00:45:26,476
All of that...

987
00:45:27,346 --> 00:45:30,346
made me feel all dispirited.

988
00:45:30,856 --> 00:45:34,486
It made me feel really...

989
00:45:42,166 --> 00:45:44,995
(The two who grew closer...)

990
00:45:44,996 --> 00:45:48,436
(after just one date)

991
00:45:50,876 --> 00:45:53,705
(The two who grew apart...)

992
00:45:53,706 --> 00:45:56,906
(after that one date)

993
00:45:59,946 --> 00:46:03,416
(Before they know it, it's deep into the night.)

994
00:46:04,116 --> 00:46:05,786
I'd better get some rest. I'm leaving.

995
00:46:05,916 --> 00:46:07,016
Bye.

996
00:46:07,316 --> 00:46:08,856
Goodnight.

997
00:46:11,026 --> 00:46:15,596
(Ye Ji and Seon Ho stay behind and clean up the playroom.)

998
00:46:18,436 --> 00:46:19,566
Did you have fun?

999
00:46:22,736 --> 00:46:24,676
You didn't even talk to me.

1000
00:46:24,936 --> 00:46:26,035
- Me?
- Yes.

1001
00:46:26,036 --> 00:46:27,846
I didn't talk to anyone.

1002
00:46:34,076 --> 00:46:36,315
- What nonsense is that?
- Did I talk to anyone?

1003
00:46:36,316 --> 00:46:38,255
Up until a few seconds ago, you were...

1004
00:46:38,256 --> 00:46:39,716
I was listening.

1005
00:46:44,426 --> 00:46:48,296
(The conversation hardly continues.)

1006
00:46:50,326 --> 00:46:52,636
We're going on another date tomorrow.

1007
00:46:56,606 --> 00:46:58,235
- Right?
- Us.

1008
00:46:58,236 --> 00:46:59,506
- Yes.
- Yes.

1009
00:47:07,686 --> 00:47:08,686
You're tired, aren't you?

1010
00:47:09,416 --> 00:47:10,446
All day...

1011
00:47:13,686 --> 00:47:17,026
I've been wanting to chat with you since earlier.

1012
00:47:18,826 --> 00:47:20,656
I was thinking of just going to bed.

1013
00:47:22,566 --> 00:47:24,496
But talking before I do...

1014
00:47:26,236 --> 00:47:28,706
seemed like the better idea.

1015
00:47:31,576 --> 00:47:36,076
(Ye Ji has asked to talk first.)

1016
00:47:37,846 --> 00:47:40,115
- How about we talk a bit later?
- Okay.

1017
00:47:40,116 --> 00:47:41,886
- Or right now?
- Yes.

1018
00:47:43,186 --> 00:47:45,615
- Okay.
- Yes, you two need to talk.

1019
00:47:45,616 --> 00:47:46,755
They have to talk...

1020
00:47:46,756 --> 00:47:48,825
- For sure.
- before tomorrow's date.

1021
00:47:48,826 --> 00:47:50,325
Please talk, you two.

1022
00:47:50,326 --> 00:47:52,656
Ye Ji, there's no time to go back now.

1023
00:47:52,896 --> 00:47:54,396
It's awkward, and very much so.

1024
00:47:55,826 --> 00:47:56,996
(Sighing)

1025
00:47:57,636 --> 00:48:01,606
(The 2 get to talk for the 1st time tonight.)

1026
00:48:05,036 --> 00:48:08,106
(Seon Ho drops by his room for a second.)

1027
00:48:10,576 --> 00:48:15,446
(He takes a jacket for Ye Ji.)

1028
00:48:16,916 --> 00:48:18,356
(Handing over)

1029
00:48:18,716 --> 00:48:19,716
No problem.

1030
00:48:20,386 --> 00:48:22,025
This jacket is thick.

1031
00:48:22,026 --> 00:48:23,485
Yes, it's thick.

1032
00:48:23,486 --> 00:48:24,726
(Ye Ji wears Seon Ho's jacket.)

1033
00:48:32,396 --> 00:48:33,736
(Glancing)

1034
00:48:37,406 --> 00:48:38,876
The night air feels nice.

1035
00:48:39,336 --> 00:48:42,306
Right? Even the sky was clear today.

1036
00:48:45,876 --> 00:48:48,116
I just wanted to ask how...

1037
00:48:49,546 --> 00:48:50,816
today went.

1038
00:48:51,616 --> 00:48:52,656
Today?

1039
00:48:56,686 --> 00:48:57,695
It was...

1040
00:48:57,696 --> 00:49:03,496
(Even the simple question is tough to answer.)

1041
00:49:05,366 --> 00:49:08,506
Honestly, here's what crossed my mind.

1042
00:49:10,236 --> 00:49:13,205
I had one person I wanted to talk to more.

1043
00:49:13,206 --> 00:49:15,446
- Was she your date today?
- Yes.

1044
00:49:15,806 --> 00:49:18,346
So I thought I'd find out today.

1045
00:49:18,576 --> 00:49:22,016
If we weren't on the same page and our conversation was mediocre,

1046
00:49:23,086 --> 00:49:25,115
there'd be...

1047
00:49:25,116 --> 00:49:27,886
one less person I'd be interested in.

1048
00:49:28,386 --> 00:49:31,226
But it...

1049
00:49:32,296 --> 00:49:33,825
When I had the lunch...

1050
00:49:33,826 --> 00:49:35,366
- Yes?
- and dinner dates,

1051
00:49:35,926 --> 00:49:38,796
the date I had at dinner was a bit more...

1052
00:49:42,136 --> 00:49:44,136
I liked the dinner date more.

1053
00:49:44,806 --> 00:49:45,806
But...

1054
00:49:47,806 --> 00:49:49,576
What confused me the most was...

1055
00:49:52,176 --> 00:49:53,915
whether I had more fun because...

1056
00:49:53,916 --> 00:49:56,146
the date course was much more enjoyable...

1057
00:49:56,646 --> 00:49:59,616
or because my date was more interesting.

1058
00:50:01,016 --> 00:50:02,186
I couldn't really tell.

1059
00:50:04,926 --> 00:50:10,696
(Seon Ho honestly expressed his current feelings.)

1060
00:50:11,796 --> 00:50:14,235
My heart sank big time.

1061
00:50:14,236 --> 00:50:16,205
I had some trust in him.

1062
00:50:16,206 --> 00:50:19,735
I thought, "No way his feelings would waver."

1063
00:50:19,736 --> 00:50:21,345
But his feelings did waver.

1064
00:50:21,346 --> 00:50:23,876
Whether it was because of his date or the atmosphere.

1065
00:50:24,516 --> 00:50:27,076
Honestly, it was a shocker.

1066
00:50:28,146 --> 00:50:29,685
So...

1067
00:50:29,686 --> 00:50:32,516
what I was worried about actually happened.

1068
00:50:33,516 --> 00:50:35,386
Despite all that,

1069
00:50:35,926 --> 00:50:38,896
we had spent time together until now.

1070
00:50:42,966 --> 00:50:44,196
Give me a moment.

1071
00:51:12,126 --> 00:51:14,355
No. Don't cry.

1072
00:51:14,356 --> 00:51:15,695
(Upset)

1073
00:51:15,696 --> 00:51:16,926
This is really upsetting.

1074
00:51:17,266 --> 00:51:18,735
It was just yesterday.

1075
00:51:18,736 --> 00:51:20,535
It was just yesterday that...

1076
00:51:20,536 --> 00:51:22,036
Seon Ho got jealous.

1077
00:51:22,206 --> 00:51:24,705
Seon Ho expressed that he had gotten jealous.

1078
00:51:24,706 --> 00:51:26,276
After hearing that,

1079
00:51:26,636 --> 00:51:29,005
Ye Ji realized that he was the jealous type...

1080
00:51:29,006 --> 00:51:30,605
and that he was interested in her.

1081
00:51:30,606 --> 00:51:32,975
Because of that, Ye Ji enjoyed the date more...

1082
00:51:32,976 --> 00:51:34,945
- the next day.
- Correct.

1083
00:51:34,946 --> 00:51:37,485
- That was during the daytime today.
- Yes.

1084
00:51:37,486 --> 00:51:40,955
With all of that going on, he suddenly said on that very night,

1085
00:51:40,956 --> 00:51:44,325
"The date I had with the girl I was curious about was..."

1086
00:51:44,326 --> 00:51:45,555
"more fun."

1087
00:51:45,556 --> 00:51:48,625
In short, in Ye Ji's shoes,

1088
00:51:48,626 --> 00:51:50,795
- it's a very upsetting situation.
- It surely is.

1089
00:51:50,796 --> 00:51:52,436
It's a heartbreaking situation.

1090
00:51:52,466 --> 00:51:54,136
Ye Ji must feel confused.

1091
00:51:59,836 --> 00:52:02,775
Talking to you was great.

1092
00:52:02,776 --> 00:52:05,816
But spending time with a different person...

1093
00:52:06,146 --> 00:52:08,616
I don't know what that means to me.

1094
00:52:08,986 --> 00:52:11,556
It's hard to judge with just one day.

1095
00:52:17,556 --> 00:52:20,926
Even I could tell that.

1096
00:52:24,736 --> 00:52:25,836
Tell what?

1097
00:52:26,236 --> 00:52:28,966
The evening date must've been memorable.

1098
00:52:29,706 --> 00:52:30,866
- I see.
- Yes.

1099
00:52:31,436 --> 00:52:33,876
Maybe, even more memorable than the daytime date.

1100
00:52:34,606 --> 00:52:36,745
- The daytime date was nice too.
- It's just that...

1101
00:52:36,746 --> 00:52:37,876
I could tell.

1102
00:52:47,156 --> 00:52:49,256
For now...

1103
00:52:54,666 --> 00:53:00,096
(The silence between the two grows longer.)

1104
00:53:02,636 --> 00:53:03,905
- Did things get complicated?
- What?

1105
00:53:03,906 --> 00:53:05,306
Did things get complicated?

1106
00:53:08,776 --> 00:53:10,176
(Thinking)

1107
00:53:11,446 --> 00:53:16,086
(Ye Ji can't answer right away.)

1108
00:53:17,386 --> 00:53:19,716
Today was, in many ways...

1109
00:53:22,526 --> 00:53:23,686
I'm sorry.

1110
00:53:23,886 --> 00:53:25,355
Why are you apologizing?

1111
00:53:25,356 --> 00:53:26,426
It's just...

1112
00:53:27,996 --> 00:53:29,566
I feel like the cause.

1113
00:53:31,566 --> 00:53:34,806
I really don't want you to mind me.

1114
00:53:37,666 --> 00:53:40,106
But it's not as if I don't mind you at all.

1115
00:53:44,346 --> 00:53:46,546
Seon Ho's feelings.

1116
00:53:47,646 --> 00:53:51,456
And my feelings. It's best to be faithful to them, no?

1117
00:53:52,456 --> 00:53:53,756
On the last day.

1118
00:53:55,226 --> 00:53:56,356
True.

1119
00:54:02,766 --> 00:54:06,965
Thank you for being honest with me.

1120
00:54:06,966 --> 00:54:09,536
Either way, you and I have a date tomorrow.

1121
00:54:11,306 --> 00:54:15,546
(Ye Ji tries hard to talk as if nothing's wrong.)

1122
00:54:16,146 --> 00:54:17,546
During the date...

1123
00:54:19,476 --> 00:54:21,486
Let's talk.

1124
00:54:25,386 --> 00:54:26,916
Wouldn't that be okay?

1125
00:54:31,926 --> 00:54:34,356
(Sighing)

1126
00:54:40,336 --> 00:54:41,906
Do you have anything more to say?

1127
00:54:42,336 --> 00:54:43,666
Shall we go inside?

1128
00:54:47,836 --> 00:54:50,575
(Faced with how different Seon Ho seemed, )

1129
00:54:50,576 --> 00:54:54,886
(Ye Ji hid her feelings.)

1130
00:54:56,816 --> 00:54:58,916
(Upset)

1131
00:55:01,526 --> 00:55:03,026
What now?

1132
00:55:03,156 --> 00:55:06,756
At least Seon Ho told Ye Ji his feelings before tomorrow's date.

1133
00:55:06,796 --> 00:55:10,425
- Even Ye Ji needed that chat.
- Yes.

1134
00:55:10,426 --> 00:55:12,065
It was much needed, but it's heartbreaking.

1135
00:55:12,066 --> 00:55:13,695
Had tomorrow come...

1136
00:55:13,696 --> 00:55:15,335
with things still up in the air...

1137
00:55:15,336 --> 00:55:16,936
- That'd be worse.
- That'd be worse.

1138
00:55:17,366 --> 00:55:18,936
She wouldn't know how to act.

1139
00:55:20,836 --> 00:55:22,006
This is tough.

1140
00:55:30,216 --> 00:55:33,886
(Before they know it, the sixth morning has arrived.)

1141
00:55:35,256 --> 00:55:36,855
What do I do?

1142
00:55:36,856 --> 00:55:39,826
I have no idea what to do during today's date.

1143
00:55:40,026 --> 00:55:43,195
What's best is to be yourself.

1144
00:55:43,196 --> 00:55:44,995
But you know...

1145
00:55:44,996 --> 00:55:46,735
It keeps bothering me.

1146
00:55:46,736 --> 00:55:49,766
The fact that his feelings are growing for someone else.

1147
00:55:50,466 --> 00:55:52,975
You shouldn't wish Seon Ho to give you a definite answer.

1148
00:55:52,976 --> 00:55:55,245
Right? He kept being wishy-washy.

1149
00:55:55,246 --> 00:55:56,745
- When I had...
- Exactly.

1150
00:55:56,746 --> 00:55:58,515
Just made up my mind yesterday,

1151
00:55:58,516 --> 00:56:00,445
- he suddenly acted all different.
- You never know.

1152
00:56:00,446 --> 00:56:02,186
It's driving me crazy.

1153
00:56:03,246 --> 00:56:04,645
Is it best to give him assurance?

1154
00:56:04,646 --> 00:56:05,755
What if he feels some pressure...

1155
00:56:05,756 --> 00:56:06,855
- You should.
- from it?

1156
00:56:06,856 --> 00:56:08,855
But stepping back now, after all this time, is a bit...

1157
00:56:08,856 --> 00:56:11,186
- Is that so?
- What you should do is...

1158
00:56:13,456 --> 00:56:16,526
What do I wear for the date?

1159
00:56:18,096 --> 00:56:19,535
(Glancing)

1160
00:56:19,536 --> 00:56:21,906
Should I wear this? It's pretty.

1161
00:56:28,776 --> 00:56:31,946
(Ye Ji leaves the room.)

1162
00:56:32,746 --> 00:56:35,015
I have a feeling...

1163
00:56:35,016 --> 00:56:39,115
Seon Ho is going through a really tough time mentally.

1164
00:56:39,116 --> 00:56:40,785
Of course. I'm sure...

1165
00:56:40,786 --> 00:56:42,862
- he's not that type of person.
- Talking to both of us...

1166
00:56:42,886 --> 00:56:45,526
Having to think about several people must be tough.

1167
00:56:51,426 --> 00:56:56,036
(Meanwhile, Seon Ho is ready for the date.)

1168
00:57:03,276 --> 00:57:06,746
(He heads to the girls' room.)

1169
00:57:11,886 --> 00:57:13,016
(Knocking)

1170
00:57:13,386 --> 00:57:14,686
(Signaling)

1171
00:57:16,226 --> 00:57:17,456
What?

1172
00:57:19,396 --> 00:57:23,496
(Seon Ho calls over Ye Ji first.)

1173
00:57:24,966 --> 00:57:28,306
(Ye Ji looks brighter.)

1174
00:57:35,806 --> 00:57:37,775
I wasn't going to let it bother me,

1175
00:57:37,776 --> 00:57:39,346
but it does bother me.

1176
00:57:41,886 --> 00:57:45,486
(Seon Ho is off on the date with Ye Ji.)

1177
00:57:48,186 --> 00:57:50,186
"Come home quickly," was what I thought.

1178
00:57:52,496 --> 00:57:55,766
(She watches the video from last night.)

1179
00:58:06,676 --> 00:58:07,676
Wait.

1180
00:58:07,677 --> 00:58:08,846
Na Young?

1181
00:58:08,976 --> 00:58:10,376
- Seriously.
- Wait.

1182
00:58:10,446 --> 00:58:11,915
How many times are you watching it?

1183
00:58:11,916 --> 00:58:12,976
Goodness.

1184
00:58:14,076 --> 00:58:15,715
She's watched that video...

1185
00:58:15,716 --> 00:58:17,386
four thousand and two hundred times.

1186
00:58:17,446 --> 00:58:18,685
(Laughing)

1187
00:58:18,686 --> 00:58:21,115
The viewers wouldn't know because of all the editing.

1188
00:58:21,116 --> 00:58:22,525
- She saw it 4,200 times?
- Yes, 4,200 times.

1189
00:58:22,526 --> 00:58:24,385
Gosh, it must be worn out by now.

1190
00:58:24,386 --> 00:58:26,756
She's going to watch it over and over again until the date.

1191
00:58:27,926 --> 00:58:30,966
(Seon Ho is all Na Young can think about.)

1192
00:58:34,096 --> 00:58:35,706
(Sighing)

1193
00:58:39,606 --> 00:58:41,275
(Yongsan-gu)

1194
00:58:41,276 --> 00:58:42,806
What great weather.

1195
00:58:46,216 --> 00:58:47,975
- Where is it? Is it on the left?
- Over there.

1196
00:58:47,976 --> 00:58:49,716
(Ye Ji and Seon Ho's last date has begun.)

1197
00:58:51,346 --> 00:58:52,756
- Let's go inside.
- Okay.

1198
00:58:53,156 --> 00:58:54,555
- Welcome.
- Hi.

1199
00:58:54,556 --> 00:58:55,885
Hi.

1200
00:58:55,886 --> 00:58:56,955
- Party for two, yes?
- Yes.

1201
00:58:56,956 --> 00:58:58,155
Choose a table, and I'll bring over the menu.

1202
00:58:58,156 --> 00:58:59,495
- Okay.
- Thank you.

1203
00:58:59,496 --> 00:59:00,655
(Their last chance to spend time together)

1204
00:59:00,656 --> 00:59:02,026
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1205
00:59:02,126 --> 00:59:03,566
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

1206
00:59:08,736 --> 00:59:11,676
(Awkward)

1207
00:59:13,136 --> 00:59:15,106
- Today's weather is so amazing...
- Yes?

1208
00:59:15,846 --> 00:59:16,946
That...

1209
00:59:17,306 --> 00:59:18,575
it feels like we're out to heal.

1210
00:59:18,576 --> 00:59:19,646
Totally.

1211
00:59:20,776 --> 00:59:24,316
How should I approach this date? What mindset should I have?

1212
00:59:24,916 --> 00:59:27,085
Should I act as if I'm fine?

1213
00:59:27,086 --> 00:59:28,985
Or should I share...

1214
00:59:28,986 --> 00:59:31,026
my heartbroken feelings?

1215
00:59:31,456 --> 00:59:32,895
After thinking things through,

1216
00:59:32,896 --> 00:59:34,955
as this was our last date,

1217
00:59:34,956 --> 00:59:38,665
I tried to act bright...

1218
00:59:38,666 --> 00:59:41,136
as if everything was fine.

1219
00:59:41,966 --> 00:59:43,065
Do you like pudding?

1220
00:59:43,066 --> 00:59:44,435
I do.

1221
00:59:44,436 --> 00:59:45,875
It's good,

1222
00:59:45,876 --> 00:59:47,996
- especially caramel pudding. Yes.
- Caramel pudding.

1223
00:59:50,006 --> 00:59:53,246
(An awkward silence follows their brief conversation.)

1224
00:59:56,316 --> 00:59:58,145
Yesterday, I was very worried...

1225
00:59:58,146 --> 01:00:00,016
A lot went through my mind.

1226
01:00:01,156 --> 01:00:02,625
(Sighing)

1227
01:00:02,626 --> 01:00:03,755
Yesterday...

1228
01:00:03,756 --> 01:00:04,786
Yes?

1229
01:00:05,326 --> 01:00:06,826
Shall we drink first?

1230
01:00:07,326 --> 01:00:08,696
Well, cheers.

1231
01:00:12,766 --> 01:00:16,166
How did you feel after our talk yesterday?

1232
01:00:17,736 --> 01:00:19,105
First of all,

1233
01:00:19,106 --> 01:00:21,175
- I was glad that we talked.
- Right.

1234
01:00:21,176 --> 01:00:23,075
If not, I would've come to the date...

1235
01:00:23,076 --> 01:00:25,176
without knowing anything.

1236
01:00:25,746 --> 01:00:28,246
Well, I'm sure it wouldn't have been much different.

1237
01:00:29,186 --> 01:00:30,246
But still,

1238
01:00:30,816 --> 01:00:33,585
I was thankful that you told me about how you felt.

1239
01:00:33,586 --> 01:00:34,586
And...

1240
01:00:35,856 --> 01:00:37,626
- it was totally understandable.
- Right.

1241
01:00:37,826 --> 01:00:41,026
Based on your character, I'm sure you felt...

1242
01:00:42,166 --> 01:00:43,895
bad about it.

1243
01:00:43,896 --> 01:00:46,866
It must have been hard even to bring it up.

1244
01:00:47,096 --> 01:00:49,366
- Right.
- I thank you for telling me.

1245
01:00:49,536 --> 01:00:50,866
But I'm fine with it.

1246
01:00:51,636 --> 01:00:54,005
It's up to you what you do.

1247
01:00:54,006 --> 01:00:55,846
- Right.
- I will do what I choose to do.

1248
01:00:56,246 --> 01:00:59,915
I hope that you won't feel bad about it.

1249
01:00:59,916 --> 01:01:02,486
We should just...

1250
01:01:04,486 --> 01:01:06,656
- Tomorrow is the last day.
- Right.

1251
01:01:06,916 --> 01:01:10,956
We should just do the best we can until that time...

1252
01:01:11,456 --> 01:01:13,756
- at our own places.
- Right.

1253
01:01:21,766 --> 01:01:23,506
You were able to meet...

1254
01:01:26,636 --> 01:01:28,876
- the others.
- Right.

1255
01:01:29,006 --> 01:01:32,416
You were able to spend time with them,

1256
01:01:32,746 --> 01:01:34,076
and I feel good about that.

1257
01:01:35,116 --> 01:01:36,116
Right.

1258
01:01:37,286 --> 01:01:38,755
I would've felt uncomfortable about it...

1259
01:01:38,756 --> 01:01:40,256
if you didn't meet the others.

1260
01:01:40,956 --> 01:01:42,686
Thank you for saying that.

1261
01:01:44,356 --> 01:01:46,696
(Letting out a sigh)

1262
01:01:46,826 --> 01:01:50,166
Do you think you spent the week without any regret?

1263
01:01:50,666 --> 01:01:52,036
Yes. Well, I thought,

1264
01:01:53,036 --> 01:01:55,136
"Would anything actually happen?"

1265
01:01:55,206 --> 01:01:57,366
I was worried before I got here.

1266
01:01:57,806 --> 01:01:58,806
Right.

1267
01:01:59,336 --> 01:02:03,046
But changes happened all of a sudden.

1268
01:02:03,546 --> 01:02:05,575
There were times...

1269
01:02:05,576 --> 01:02:08,416
when I suffered emotionally.

1270
01:02:08,516 --> 01:02:10,946
There were good days as well. I went through mood swings...

1271
01:02:11,446 --> 01:02:13,515
within just one week.

1272
01:02:13,516 --> 01:02:15,526
It was as if I was on a roller coaster.

1273
01:02:15,926 --> 01:02:18,526
My feelings went up and down.

1274
01:02:18,996 --> 01:02:21,496
That made me feel surprised about myself.

1275
01:02:22,296 --> 01:02:24,026
Actually,

1276
01:02:24,496 --> 01:02:27,295
if I look back through my life,

1277
01:02:27,296 --> 01:02:30,636
I wasn't able to approach someone first to express my feelings.

1278
01:02:30,966 --> 01:02:34,435
I was someone who always kept my feelings hidden.

1279
01:02:34,436 --> 01:02:35,906
- Right.
- But...

1280
01:02:37,076 --> 01:02:39,876
we're in an extreme situation.

1281
01:02:40,246 --> 01:02:42,386
No matter how timid I was,

1282
01:02:42,986 --> 01:02:45,956
I had to be active and ask for a conversation.

1283
01:02:46,356 --> 01:02:47,986
I had to express myself.

1284
01:02:48,526 --> 01:02:52,326
My actions felt so unfamiliar.

1285
01:02:53,326 --> 01:02:57,126
I wasn't sure if it was right to start a conversation.

1286
01:02:57,966 --> 01:03:00,235
No. I felt thankful that you started a conversation with me.

1287
01:03:00,236 --> 01:03:02,436
- After talking with you, - Yes.

1288
01:03:02,906 --> 01:03:04,806
I was glad that we talked.

1289
01:03:05,476 --> 01:03:07,536
I wanted to tell you anyway.

1290
01:03:07,776 --> 01:03:09,845
If we didn't have a conversation yesterday,

1291
01:03:09,846 --> 01:03:12,176
- I was going to tell you today.
- Right.

1292
01:03:12,546 --> 01:03:16,486
I knew how you were going to feel.

1293
01:03:17,046 --> 01:03:19,916
It would've been tough to bring it up today.

1294
01:03:20,056 --> 01:03:22,586
You started a conversation with me yesterday,

1295
01:03:23,056 --> 01:03:26,596
and that became an opportunity to talk about that.

1296
01:03:27,526 --> 01:03:31,566
It would've been something upsetting to hear,

1297
01:03:31,936 --> 01:03:34,166
but you listened to what I had to say.

1298
01:03:36,106 --> 01:03:37,136
It felt like...

1299
01:03:37,866 --> 01:03:39,206
- you understood me.
- Right.

1300
01:03:41,276 --> 01:03:43,006
Well,

1301
01:03:43,806 --> 01:03:45,476
I'm in the same position.

1302
01:03:46,716 --> 01:03:49,746
Anyone could feel curious.

1303
01:03:51,446 --> 01:03:53,606
We have limited time to spend with each other as well.

1304
01:04:02,366 --> 01:04:06,066
We should carry on...

1305
01:04:07,436 --> 01:04:09,756
with the heart we'll feel at the final moment of tomorrow.

1306
01:04:15,846 --> 01:04:17,646
Let's do our best until tomorrow.

1307
01:04:27,916 --> 01:04:29,056
What?

1308
01:04:30,656 --> 01:04:32,832
- They're not breaking up, are they?
- Why does it feel sad?

1309
01:04:32,856 --> 01:04:34,955
Why do they sound like people breaking up?

1310
01:04:34,956 --> 01:04:36,126
- Right.
- Right.

1311
01:04:36,626 --> 01:04:38,736
It doesn't feel like a date. They're both thinking,

1312
01:04:38,936 --> 01:04:41,696
"Must it be that way?"

1313
01:04:41,966 --> 01:04:43,065
"Must I do that for him or her?"

1314
01:04:43,066 --> 01:04:45,475
It feels like a duty.

1315
01:04:45,476 --> 01:04:46,575
- Right.
- Right.

1316
01:04:46,576 --> 01:04:48,175
- Why?
- It ended up like this...

1317
01:04:48,176 --> 01:04:50,276
- after last night.
- Right.

1318
01:04:50,706 --> 01:04:52,315
- It's not a date.
- They feel bad for each other.

1319
01:04:52,316 --> 01:04:53,316
They feel bad for each other.

1320
01:04:53,317 --> 01:04:54,575
They keep feeling that way.

1321
01:04:54,576 --> 01:04:55,962
But there's no need for them to feel that way.

1322
01:04:55,986 --> 01:04:58,546
(Feeling upset)

1323
01:04:59,956 --> 01:05:01,656
(Sighing)

1324
01:05:09,266 --> 01:05:13,836
(Kim Seon Ho and Jung Ye Ji's date has come to an end.)

1325
01:05:14,466 --> 01:05:15,966
It ended really quickly today.

1326
01:05:17,266 --> 01:05:20,736
(The two of them received the final text message.)

1327
01:05:21,576 --> 01:05:23,346
Do you feel sad about it?

1328
01:05:23,446 --> 01:05:24,675
I do.

1329
01:05:24,676 --> 01:05:26,076
I want to stay here longer.

1330
01:05:32,186 --> 01:05:33,656
- I wish we had more time.
- Right.

1331
01:05:56,476 --> 01:05:58,106
You're such a busy guy.

1332
01:05:59,946 --> 01:06:01,516
- So busy.
- Right.

1333
01:06:02,986 --> 01:06:04,086
Gosh.

1334
01:06:07,316 --> 01:06:09,626
Anyway, have a good time today.

1335
01:06:10,986 --> 01:06:13,026
- Right. I'll see you later.
- Right.

1336
01:06:14,226 --> 01:06:16,166
I'll see you at the House.

1337
01:06:18,496 --> 01:06:20,135
- Rest up well.
- Okay.

1338
01:06:20,136 --> 01:06:23,366
(Time went by faster than ever.)

1339
01:06:24,136 --> 01:06:25,936
There's a car coming. Let's move slowly.

1340
01:06:27,436 --> 01:06:32,006
(Their last date has come to an end.)

1341
01:06:34,346 --> 01:06:35,985
(The House at that time)

1342
01:06:35,986 --> 01:06:38,086
- I thought you were in college.
- Really?

1343
01:06:39,016 --> 01:06:40,355
- Really?
- You look so young.

1344
01:06:40,356 --> 01:06:41,415
Really?

1345
01:06:41,416 --> 01:06:42,762
(Ryun Gi and Ro Bin head out for their date.)

1346
01:06:42,786 --> 01:06:44,656
- The weather is so nice.
- Hey, take my hand.

1347
01:06:45,026 --> 01:06:47,826
(Holding)

1348
01:06:48,126 --> 01:06:49,166
Done.

1349
01:06:50,496 --> 01:06:52,595
It feels like Animal Crossing with these two.

1350
01:06:52,596 --> 01:06:54,165
- Right!
- Right.

1351
01:06:54,166 --> 01:06:55,636
It's a therapeutic moment.

1352
01:06:55,736 --> 01:06:56,966
"Hey, take my hand."

1353
01:06:58,036 --> 01:06:59,275
She's such a teto-girl.

1354
01:06:59,276 --> 01:07:00,875
Ryun Gi's heart...

1355
01:07:00,876 --> 01:07:02,375
- is set toward her.
- He feels so happy.

1356
01:07:02,376 --> 01:07:03,376
- Right.
- Right.

1357
01:07:03,377 --> 01:07:05,615
Ro Bin would've felt that.

1358
01:07:05,616 --> 01:07:07,646
- Right.
- Will she see him as a friend...

1359
01:07:07,846 --> 01:07:10,416
or will she start to develop feelings for him?

1360
01:07:10,516 --> 01:07:11,985
Ryun Gi should keep knocking at the door of her heart...

1361
01:07:11,986 --> 01:07:13,255
- without giving up.
- Right.

1362
01:07:13,256 --> 01:07:14,536
- He should keep it up.
- Right.

1363
01:07:14,756 --> 01:07:18,755
I hope she slowly plunges into his charms.

1364
01:07:18,756 --> 01:07:19,926
- Slowly.
- Right.

1365
01:07:21,096 --> 01:07:22,196
- Okay.
- Let's go.

1366
01:07:25,666 --> 01:07:27,766
- The weather is great.
- The weather is so nice.

1367
01:07:28,196 --> 01:07:30,266
- It'll be perfect without the wind.
- Right.

1368
01:07:30,806 --> 01:07:31,935
- You're the weather fairy.
- The wind...

1369
01:07:31,936 --> 01:07:35,676
The wind feels warm. It feels nice today.

1370
01:07:36,506 --> 01:07:38,876
Right. It feels warmer than yesterday.

1371
01:07:39,246 --> 01:07:40,276
Right.

1372
01:07:40,976 --> 01:07:42,046
The weather is...

1373
01:07:42,986 --> 01:07:44,046
much better.

1374
01:07:44,386 --> 01:07:46,756
(Yongsan-gu)

1375
01:07:48,316 --> 01:07:51,386
(A cute restaurant that suits the two)

1376
01:07:53,026 --> 01:07:54,026
Karashi.

1377
01:07:54,496 --> 01:07:56,326
- Karashi.
- Japanese vibes.

1378
01:07:58,226 --> 01:07:59,266
I love it.

1379
01:08:01,536 --> 01:08:02,936
Hello.

1380
01:08:03,736 --> 01:08:04,736
- Hello.
- Hello.

1381
01:08:04,737 --> 01:08:06,335
Sit to the left.

1382
01:08:06,336 --> 01:08:07,476
- Here?
- Yes.

1383
01:08:08,606 --> 01:08:11,306
The weather is so nice.

1384
01:08:12,746 --> 01:08:13,876
Thank you.

1385
01:08:16,346 --> 01:08:17,416
What should we have?

1386
01:08:20,616 --> 01:08:21,685
Awesome.

1387
01:08:21,686 --> 01:08:23,186
(Focused)

1388
01:08:23,926 --> 01:08:25,256
- This.
- Right.

1389
01:08:26,096 --> 01:08:28,026
- Should we do that?
- Right. Let's do that.

1390
01:08:28,526 --> 01:08:30,766
Okay. Do you want any drinks?

1391
01:08:33,666 --> 01:08:35,666
They must not have regular soft drinks.

1392
01:08:35,836 --> 01:08:37,766
- They don't?
- They're all alcoholic drinks.

1393
01:08:38,606 --> 01:08:40,476
There are non-alcoholic drinks as well.

1394
01:08:40,576 --> 01:08:41,605
Where?

1395
01:08:41,606 --> 01:08:44,175
There's the non-alcoholic highball.

1396
01:08:44,176 --> 01:08:46,146
- Coke and Coke Zero.
- Gosh.

1397
01:08:46,446 --> 01:08:47,916
Should we get a Coke Zero?

1398
01:08:48,516 --> 01:08:50,916
- Should we get a Coke Zero?
- Sure.

1399
01:08:51,686 --> 01:08:54,585
We'll get these two...

1400
01:08:54,586 --> 01:08:56,986
- and a Coke Zero, please.
- Right.

1401
01:08:57,326 --> 01:08:58,356
Thank you.

1402
01:09:01,326 --> 01:09:03,666
- The weather is so nice.
- Right.

1403
01:09:07,336 --> 01:09:09,036
- How do you feel?
- About what?

1404
01:09:09,606 --> 01:09:11,436
- It's the last day tomorrow.
- Right.

1405
01:09:12,506 --> 01:09:14,735
It's going to be hectic tomorrow.

1406
01:09:14,736 --> 01:09:16,345
- We won't be able to spend time.
- Right.

1407
01:09:16,346 --> 01:09:18,006
Today is an important day, isn't it?

1408
01:09:20,376 --> 01:09:21,445
What do you think?

1409
01:09:21,446 --> 01:09:22,585
- Me?
- Yes.

1410
01:09:22,586 --> 01:09:23,746
Did time go by quickly?

1411
01:09:24,616 --> 01:09:26,056
It did.

1412
01:09:26,386 --> 01:09:28,516
Time went by quickly, and it felt too short.

1413
01:09:28,926 --> 01:09:29,955
- Right.
- Right.

1414
01:09:29,956 --> 01:09:32,796
That is why I have a lot going through my head.

1415
01:09:34,956 --> 01:09:36,602
- What about you?
- You have a lot to think about?

1416
01:09:36,626 --> 01:09:37,626
Me?

1417
01:09:37,627 --> 01:09:38,666
Well,

1418
01:09:39,066 --> 01:09:40,496
I do have a lot to think about.

1419
01:09:43,136 --> 01:09:44,166
Well,

1420
01:09:45,676 --> 01:09:47,036
when I went...

1421
01:09:47,676 --> 01:09:50,876
to do the laundry yesterday,

1422
01:09:51,506 --> 01:09:53,376
things became clear for me.

1423
01:09:53,546 --> 01:09:56,246
- Really?
- I felt that I didn't have to...

1424
01:09:56,546 --> 01:09:58,215
- think anymore.
- Right.

1425
01:09:58,216 --> 01:10:00,016
(I felt that I didn't have to think anymore.)

1426
01:10:01,216 --> 01:10:04,156
That is why I don't have that much to think about.

1427
01:10:05,186 --> 01:10:07,626
(Surprised)

1428
01:10:07,726 --> 01:10:10,126
(He shares his certainty toward Ro Bin.)

1429
01:10:10,296 --> 01:10:13,336
Thank you so much for being honest about it.

1430
01:10:15,166 --> 01:10:16,265
- You should think about it.
- Right.

1431
01:10:16,266 --> 01:10:18,335
It's right for you to think about it.

1432
01:10:18,336 --> 01:10:20,976
But today, I want to have fun with you...

1433
01:10:21,236 --> 01:10:23,906
without thinking about anything else.

1434
01:10:24,846 --> 01:10:27,645
- That can't happen.
- Why not?

1435
01:10:27,646 --> 01:10:29,385
- You can't go completely blank.
- No.

1436
01:10:29,386 --> 01:10:32,045
- Well, the complicated thoughts.
- Good.

1437
01:10:32,046 --> 01:10:33,726
- I was joking. That sounds good.
- Right.

1438
01:10:34,456 --> 01:10:35,685
- Let's try later.
- Oh, right.

1439
01:10:35,686 --> 01:10:37,886
Thank you.

1440
01:10:38,586 --> 01:10:39,996
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1441
01:10:44,226 --> 01:10:47,336
It's been a really long time since I've had Coke Zero.

1442
01:10:48,366 --> 01:10:50,306
- You don't drink carbonated drinks?
- I don't.

1443
01:10:50,406 --> 01:10:52,035
What? I also don't drink carbonated drinks.

1444
01:10:52,036 --> 01:10:53,036
Really?

1445
01:10:53,776 --> 01:10:55,182
You ordered this because of me, right?

1446
01:10:55,206 --> 01:10:56,375
Yes. What about you?

1447
01:10:56,376 --> 01:10:58,006
I ordered it because of you.

1448
01:10:58,106 --> 01:11:00,316
Should we get whatever we want to drink?

1449
01:11:01,146 --> 01:11:02,215
Let's do that.

1450
01:11:02,216 --> 01:11:03,762
(They ordered the drink for each other.)

1451
01:11:03,786 --> 01:11:05,446
You two are really close.

1452
01:11:05,546 --> 01:11:06,956
- Gosh!
- Right.

1453
01:11:07,586 --> 01:11:09,556
You two are touching! You two are about to touch!

1454
01:11:11,556 --> 01:11:12,895
Ryun Gi looks comfortable.

1455
01:11:12,896 --> 01:11:15,226
Right. A lot more comfortable. How cute!

1456
01:11:15,396 --> 01:11:18,996
When you see considerate couples,

1457
01:11:19,096 --> 01:11:20,565
there are times when...

1458
01:11:20,566 --> 01:11:22,295
they order things for each other while assuming that...

1459
01:11:22,296 --> 01:11:24,066
- Right.
- they would like them.

1460
01:11:25,306 --> 01:11:27,226
They would both eat things that they don't like.

1461
01:11:29,046 --> 01:11:31,105
Isn't this something you can't have?

1462
01:11:31,106 --> 01:11:33,575
To be honest, I can't drink it. I can't have carbonated drinks.

1463
01:11:33,576 --> 01:11:35,376
- I'll drink it.
- Just pour it for me.

1464
01:11:35,646 --> 01:11:36,746
Okay.

1465
01:11:37,146 --> 01:11:39,516
- Hey!
- What is it?

1466
01:11:40,786 --> 01:11:42,626
Shall we clink our glasses?

1467
01:11:45,426 --> 01:11:46,956
(Taking a bite)

1468
01:11:48,926 --> 01:11:50,726
(Taking a bite)

1469
01:11:52,496 --> 01:11:53,535
Actually,

1470
01:11:53,536 --> 01:11:55,665
- I wanted to ask you this.
- What is it?

1471
01:11:55,666 --> 01:11:58,605
I wasn't able to bring it up...

1472
01:11:58,606 --> 01:12:00,636
- as it was something personal.
- Right.

1473
01:12:00,876 --> 01:12:02,975
If I remember it correctly,

1474
01:12:02,976 --> 01:12:05,145
you said your father was watching over you from above.

1475
01:12:05,146 --> 01:12:06,745
May I ask when he left?

1476
01:12:06,746 --> 01:12:08,316
It was when I was in ninth grade.

1477
01:12:08,416 --> 01:12:09,586
My dad...

1478
01:12:11,116 --> 01:12:12,715
didn't suffer from an illness.

1479
01:12:12,716 --> 01:12:15,586
He just passed away all of a sudden.

1480
01:12:17,356 --> 01:12:19,895
There was no specific cause? It was just an acute disease?

1481
01:12:19,896 --> 01:12:21,456
Right.

1482
01:12:22,056 --> 01:12:24,366
Back then,

1483
01:12:25,326 --> 01:12:29,135
I was young, but I was old enough to know what was going on.

1484
01:12:29,136 --> 01:12:32,936
It happened so suddenly,

1485
01:12:33,736 --> 01:12:35,176
so...

1486
01:12:36,706 --> 01:12:40,615
I started to fall into darkness...

1487
01:12:40,616 --> 01:12:41,676
since then.

1488
01:12:42,376 --> 01:12:44,346
After my dad passed away,

1489
01:12:44,446 --> 01:12:47,086
I didn't know how to express my feelings.

1490
01:12:48,216 --> 01:12:50,726
All of my family members felt very sad.

1491
01:12:51,226 --> 01:12:53,956
I've never heard those sounds of wailing before.

1492
01:12:54,296 --> 01:12:57,066
The sounds of their wailing were a great shock to me.

1493
01:12:57,166 --> 01:12:58,766
As they were a great shock to me,

1494
01:12:59,636 --> 01:13:03,506
I didn't want to make those shocking sounds with them.

1495
01:13:03,606 --> 01:13:05,666
That was why I didn't cry.

1496
01:13:06,276 --> 01:13:07,506
But...

1497
01:13:08,676 --> 01:13:13,316
my family wanted to know...

1498
01:13:14,676 --> 01:13:16,515
why I didn't cry.

1499
01:13:16,516 --> 01:13:19,286
I think I tried to avoid that situation.

1500
01:13:20,956 --> 01:13:21,956
Well,

1501
01:13:23,356 --> 01:13:24,985
I'm not sure.

1502
01:13:24,986 --> 01:13:28,226
I don't know how to describe that emotion.

1503
01:13:28,596 --> 01:13:30,396
Even I struggle to understand what it was.

1504
01:13:32,866 --> 01:13:34,296
After I got sick,

1505
01:13:34,396 --> 01:13:37,866
there was a time when I cried my eyes out.

1506
01:13:38,136 --> 01:13:39,576
But at that moment,

1507
01:13:39,676 --> 01:13:42,236
the things stuck inside my heart were released.

1508
01:13:43,276 --> 01:13:46,016
I started to cry a lot more after that moment.

1509
01:13:46,776 --> 01:13:49,746
But I still struggle to cry in front of others.

1510
01:13:52,346 --> 01:13:54,816
That must be why...

1511
01:13:55,926 --> 01:13:58,285
your mother loved you twice as more.

1512
01:13:58,286 --> 01:14:00,556
My mom? Right.

1513
01:14:00,656 --> 01:14:02,966
My sisters did a lot for me as well.

1514
01:14:03,426 --> 01:14:05,166
- Right.
- Right.

1515
01:14:07,866 --> 01:14:11,266
I prepared these this morning.

1516
01:14:12,036 --> 01:14:13,676
These postcards...

1517
01:14:13,836 --> 01:14:16,275
- were picked with great care.
- Right.

1518
01:14:16,276 --> 01:14:20,376
I bought these based on the images...

1519
01:14:20,776 --> 01:14:23,546
- of the people in the House.
- Right.

1520
01:14:23,716 --> 01:14:26,355
They each hold a special meaning.

1521
01:14:26,356 --> 01:14:28,056
- I got this one.
- That's amazing of you.

1522
01:14:28,486 --> 01:14:29,786
Will you give these out today?

1523
01:14:30,486 --> 01:14:31,555
Yes. After writing in each one.

1524
01:14:31,556 --> 01:14:32,896
- Really?
- Yes.

1525
01:14:33,726 --> 01:14:35,195
Are you serious?

1526
01:14:35,196 --> 01:14:38,296
- Who do you think this is?
- Right.

1527
01:14:39,836 --> 01:14:41,366
Who could it be?

1528
01:14:42,166 --> 01:14:43,166
This is you.

1529
01:14:43,306 --> 01:14:44,936
- Why?
- What?

1530
01:14:45,266 --> 01:14:48,576
I told you this. Your first impression...

1531
01:14:48,836 --> 01:14:50,946
- felt pure and clear.
- Gosh!

1532
01:14:51,306 --> 01:14:52,345
Gosh!

1533
01:14:52,346 --> 01:14:53,576
I didn't finish writing them,

1534
01:14:54,416 --> 01:14:56,316
but I wrote yours first in the morning.

1535
01:14:56,546 --> 01:14:58,015
(Surprised)

1536
01:14:58,016 --> 01:15:00,585
I was going to give it to you last, but we had our date today.

1537
01:15:00,586 --> 01:15:01,716
When should I read it?

1538
01:15:03,186 --> 01:15:04,425
- You can read it now.
- Really?

1539
01:15:04,426 --> 01:15:05,755
You can read it now.

1540
01:15:05,756 --> 01:15:07,555
I was going to give it to you last,

1541
01:15:07,556 --> 01:15:10,696
but I prepared it before coming out this morning.

1542
01:15:10,796 --> 01:15:12,025
- I wrote it in advance.
- Gosh!

1543
01:15:12,026 --> 01:15:13,065
(Ryun Gi wrote a letter for Ro Bin.)

1544
01:15:13,066 --> 01:15:14,996
Your handwriting is so nice.

1545
01:15:15,096 --> 01:15:17,335
What? I scribbled the words.

1546
01:15:17,336 --> 01:15:18,435
(To Ro Bin)

1547
01:15:18,436 --> 01:15:19,775
(Hi, Ro Bin.)

1548
01:15:19,776 --> 01:15:22,416
(You are someone who gives off the beautiful love of your family.)

1549
01:15:22,806 --> 01:15:25,205
(You are a comfortable person who makes me forget my pain, )

1550
01:15:25,206 --> 01:15:31,386
(and it always makes me feel amazed and grateful.)

1551
01:15:31,716 --> 01:15:38,686
(I hope our relationship lasts for a long time.)

1552
01:15:39,556 --> 01:15:41,226
This is awesome, Ryun Gi.

1553
01:15:42,556 --> 01:15:43,566
This is awesome.

1554
01:15:44,796 --> 01:15:46,896
The very first gift.

1555
01:15:47,966 --> 01:15:50,865
Thank you so much. I didn't prepare anything for you.

1556
01:15:50,866 --> 01:15:52,205
You didn't have to.

1557
01:15:52,206 --> 01:15:54,475
Really? Gosh.

1558
01:15:54,476 --> 01:15:57,676
(Ryun Gi shared his heart through the letter.)

1559
01:15:58,746 --> 01:16:00,876
Thank you, Ryun Gi.

1560
01:16:02,446 --> 01:16:05,016
My heart fluttered the most when I got his letter.

1561
01:16:05,516 --> 01:16:08,256
He calmly explained...

1562
01:16:08,516 --> 01:16:10,656
why he chose the postcard.

1563
01:16:11,756 --> 01:16:13,496
He felt attractive as a man,

1564
01:16:13,696 --> 01:16:16,826
and it made me want to know more about him.

1565
01:16:18,966 --> 01:16:21,495
Most importantly,

